\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\f0\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 where 
\i fd
\i0  is the file descriptor that prompted the function call and 
\i userData
\i0  is the same pointer that was passed as the third argument to 
\b DPSAddFD()
\b0 .  The 
\i userData
\i0  pointer is provided as a convenience, allowing you to pass arbitrary data to 
\i handler
\i0 . \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 DPSRemoveFD()
\b0  removes the specified file descriptor from the list of those that the application will check.  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 Typically, 
\b DPSAddFD()
\b0  is used to listen to a socket or pipe; it's rarely used to monitor a common file.\

