\b0  functions, except that rather than wait for all PostScript code to execute, it returns immediately, allowing your application to procede while the PostScript code is executed in the background.  The DPSPingProc function 
\i handler
\i0  is called (with 
\i context
\i0  and 
\i userData
\i0  as its two arguments) when all the PostScript code has been executed.  The DPSPingProc function takes the form\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx3140\tx3900\tx4400\tx4900\tx5400\tx5920\tx6420\tx6920\tx7420\tx7920\tx8440\tx8940\tx9440\tx9940\tx10440\tx10960\f3\fs24\li2760\fc0\cf0 void *
\i handler
