\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\f0\b0\fs28\fi-1560\li2380\fc0\cf0 SUMMARY	Set the function that filters events\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1960 DECLARED IN	dpsclient/dpsNeXT.h\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1940\li2760 SYNOPSIS	DPSEventFilterFunc 
\b DPSSetEventFunc(
\b0 DPSContext 
\i context
\i0 , DPSEventFilterFunc€
\i func
\b\i0 )\

\fs30 \

\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380 DESCRIPTION	
\b DPSSetEventFunc()
\b0  establishes the function 
\i func
\i0  as the function to be called when an event record is returned from the PostScript context 
\i context
\i0  in the Window Server.  The registered function is called before the event record is put in the event queue.  If the registered function returns 0, the record is discarded.  If the registered function returns 1, the record is passed on for further processing.\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 Only event records coming from the Window Server are filtered by the registered function.  Records that you post to the event queue using 
\b DPSPostEvent()
\b0  aren't affected.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 A DPSEventFilterFunc function takes the following form:\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx3140\tx3900\tx4400\tx4900\tx5400\tx5920\tx6420\tx6920\tx7420\tx7920\tx8440\tx8940\tx9440\tx9940\tx10440\tx10960\f3\fs24\li2760\fc0\cf0 int *
\i func
\i0 (NXEvent *
\i anEvent
\i0 )\

\fs30 \

\pard\tx2380\f0\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	
\b DPSSetEventFunc()
\b0  returns a pointer to the previously registered event function.  This lets you chain together the current and previous event functions.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\fs28\fi-1540 SEE ALSO
\b 	DPSPostEvent()\

\fs20 \

\fs60 \

